        "Abu Dharr (RA) eventually requested permission to retire to al-Rabadhah, a desolate outpost outside Madinah, to avoid the tribulations (fitna) he feared were coming. He lived there in extreme simplicity with his wife and a servant. In 32 AH, as he lay dying, he had no shroud to be buried in. A group of travelers, including Abdullah ibn Mas'ud (RA), happened to pass by and discovered the dying lion of Islam. They wept as they fulfilled the Prophet’s ﷺ prophecy, washing and burying the man who had lived his entire life in the shadow of the Hereafter.",
