        "Al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam (RA) occupies a position of singular distinction in the annals of Islamic history. Born in Makkah around 594 CE, he was the son of Al-Awwam ibn Khuwaylid and Safiyyah bint Abd al-Muttalib (RA), making him the nephew of Khadijah (RA) and the first cousin of the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ. Known for his tall stature, immense physical strength, and unwavering courage, Al-Zubayr (RA) was one of the As-Sabiqun al-Awwalun (the first to embrace Islam), accepting the faith at the tender age of fifteen through the invitation of Abu Bakr al-Siddiq (RA). His conversion marked the beginning of a life dedicated entirely to the defense and propagation of the Deen.",
